# Arms and Equipment Guide objects that Forgotten Realms Campaign Setting (3.5) also define(s) (3.5 reprint): loaded only when none of those books is loaded.
Claw Bracer												PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Claw Bracer																TYPE:Bracer.Weapon.Exotic.Melee.Light.Finesseable.Piercing		CONTAINS:UNLIM|Weapon Crystal=1							COST:30	WT:2										CRITMULT:x2	CRITRANGE:2							DAMAGE:1d4				EQMOD:STEEL					WIELD:Light											SIZE:M	SOURCEPAGE:p.6																									SPROP:A claw bracer is a metal armband with three steel claws projecting from the top, extending about 4 inches beyond the tip of the wearer's extended fingers. The wearer can cast spells normally while wearing the bracer and cannot be disarmed. Many claw bracers are enhanced as magic weapons.
Khopesh												PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Khopesh																	TYPE:Weapon.Exotic.Melee.OneHanded.Slashing				CONTAINS:UNLIM|Weapon Crystal=1							COST:20	WT:12										CRITMULT:x2	CRITRANGE:2							DAMAGE:1d8				EQMOD:STEEL					WIELD:OneHanded										SIZE:M	SOURCEPAGE:p.8																									SPROP:You can use a khopesh to make trip attacks with its hooklike blade. If you are tripped during your own trip attempt, you can drop the khopesh to avoid being tripped.
Chakram												PROFICIENCY:WEAPON|Chakram																	TYPE:Weapon.Exotic.Ranged.Thrown.Slashing					CONTAINS:UNLIM|Weapon Crystal=1							COST:50	WT:2										CRITMULT:x3	CRITRANGE:1							DAMAGE:1d4				EQMOD:STEEL					WIELD:Light									RANGE:30	SIZE:M	SOURCEPAGE:p.6																									SPROP:The chakram is a throwing disk or quoit about 1 foot in diameter, with a sharpened outer rim.
Hammock																																	TYPE:Goods.General																				COST:5	WT:1																																													SOURCEPAGE:p.23																									SPROP:This portable sling is a favorite of sailors and rangers. It is hung up between two posts or trees to create a comfortable bed that is off the ground.
Insect Netting																																TYPE:Goods.General																				COST:200	WT:5																																													SOURCEPAGE:p.24																									SPROP:This is a 10-foot-by-20-foot rectangle of very light woven fabric designed to keep small insects from getting through. If properly set up, it keeps away mosquitoes, bees, and other ordinary vermin. It does not prevent monstrous vermin from getting through. See the beekeeper's outfit under Class Tools and Skill Kits for more information.
Marbles																																	TYPE:Goods.General																				COST:0.2	WT:2																																													SOURCEPAGE:p.24																									SPROP:About two dozen assorted glass, flawed rock crystal, or clay spheres in a leather pouch. They are commonly used as toys but are also useful for checking the slope in a dungeon corridor (just set one down and see which way it rolls), or as a nondamaging alternative to caltrops. One bag covers an area 5 feet square. Creatures moving through or fighting in the area must make Balance checks (DC 15). A creature that fails is unable to move for 1 round (or may fall; see the Balance skill description in the Player's Handbook). The DM judges the effectiveness of marbles against unusual opponents. Creatures that are Huge or larger tend to crush the marbles into dust, while those with multiple legs, like carrion crawlers, can scramble along without falling.
